Dragontamer wrote:
> I can't seem to find a central source of information regarding how
> different items can get burnt and how to beat fire traps. So my
> first question is, does anyone know if one exists?
> 
> Second, how do you prevent fire traps from activating?

Don't step on them. Seriously, it's better to detect the trap in advance
(ring of searching, Excalibur, intrinsic searching, wand of secret door
detection (works I think), confused gold detection for a complete level
(but there's a better use for the scrolls in the Endgame), etc...) and
circumvent it or dig around it. I think I've seem that it's possible to
jump (by use of boots, spell, or intrinsic (Knight)) across such a trap
without triggering it, but I am not quite sure about it.

> I'd assume
> levitation would be good, but I'm currently playing as a ranger and
> levitation pretty much disables multi-shot.

Levitation does not work.

> Third, is there any chance that items in a BoH can get burnt from
> a fire trap? I know that water can wipe out scrolls / potions (learned
> it unfortunately... the hard way) so can fire do the same thing?

Potions may boil, scrolls and books may burn, wooden/clothen armor may
burn if carried in the open inventory, but all are safe in a bag.

If you're already fire resistant you can also just fireproof your armor
and just cross the trap and ignore it's effect, as long as you don't
carry (mainly) potions/scrolls in your open inventory, which is good to
do, anyway, because your items may be affected by a dragon beath.

> Finally, I keep a habit of having emergency scrolls and potions open
> in my inventory (teleport and extra/full healing). They tend to burn/
> boil
> when I get hit by a trap. So are there any random tips to either
> prevent
> fire traps from effecting them, or how to stop fire traps in general?

You can't disable firetraps. Keep your burnable items in a sack or bag;
always. Replace teleport scrolls by the respective wand (at least once
you reached Gehennom).

And keep in mind that also magic traps occasionally emit a fire burst.

